      "sourceLanguage": "en",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.35,
          "end": 3.92,
          "en": "In this chapter, we will be talking about mounds and volumes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.95,
          "end": 6.47,
          "en": "You will learn how does a volume work?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.47,
          "end": 8.24,
          "en": "How does a file system work?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.27,
          "end": 10.25,
          "en": "What do mounds do?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.52,
          "end": 16.55,
          "en": "They pretty much enable you that you can access additional media, for example, external media or internal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.85,
          "end": 17.66,
          "en": "drives?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.87,
          "end": 20.75,
          "en": "So we will have a look at how those mounds work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.44,
          "end": 28.4,
          "en": "You will learn how you can use the file access tab to permanently declare those mounds so they can be,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.4,
          "end": 31.94,
          "en": "for example, automatically created for you on boot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.94,
          "end": 39.56,
          "en": "This will allow you, for example, to have multiple drives in your file system, for example, because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 39.56,
          "end": 45.2,
          "en": "maybe one drive doesn't have enough storage and then you can extend that with another drive and you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 45.2,
          "end": 52.64,
          "en": "can declare that in the access tab and we will see how you can mount external, for example, FTP servers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 52.64,
          "end": 54.26,
          "en": "into your file system.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 54.26,
          "end": 61.17,
          "en": "And this will allow you to use all the existing command line tools with an external FTP server and this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 61.17,
          "end": 62.67,
          "en": "is extremely powerful.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 63.18,
          "end": 67.2,
          "en": "In addition, there will be a really important practical example here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 67.2,
          "end": 72.71000000000001,
          "en": "I will teach you how you can deal with a broken file system to still access your data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 72.72,
          "end": 79.38,
          "en": "This will prepare you for, for example, if in the future you are the sysadmin of a computer and the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 79.38,
          "end": 82.23,
          "en": "hard disk dies or there's a problem there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 82.23,
          "end": 83.46000000000001,
          "en": "But it's somewhat working.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 83.46000000000001,
          "end": 88.41,
          "en": "But it the for example, it, it it just doesn't work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 88.41,
          "end": 94.38,
          "en": "You can't access the data, but the hard drive is still spinning and in general still functioning.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 95.00999999999999,
          "end": 96.9,
          "en": "This happens from time to time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 97.53,
          "end": 105.15,
          "en": "And I will teach you how you can deal with that and how you can try to recover the data then from that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 105.15,
          "end": 105.53999999999999,
          "en": "drive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 105.53999999999999,
          "end": 108.57,
          "en": "So let's start with the beginning.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 108.57,
          "end": 115.25999999999999,
          "en": "Let's start with the structure of how such a storage device works and how we can inspect that.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
